WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.270
Here it comes. That's the plane.

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:07.310
How must he feel, seeing Mt. Fuji
 for the first time in 28 years?

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.350
A man who didn't know the war ended
 and kept fighting.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.770
He has returned to his home country.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.990
(February, the 47st of Shinka Era
 Haneda Airport)

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.400
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:41.230
I heard it
 A voice cursing fate

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.560
I found it
 A way to use my power

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:49.520
What you want are not words,
 are they?

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.810
This love of mine
 You can have it

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.270
Humans are weak

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.940
Understanding is
 proof of determination

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.310
Come on Wakers. Ready, go!

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:07.310
Protecting the illusions
 that somebody dreamed of

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:11.650
People laugh, saying it's pointless

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:22.690
Everyone wants to live
 on someone else's justice

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:28.650
What can I do in this
 hopeless world we live in?

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:33.100
Only those that keep searching

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:39.980
can find the hero

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.000
(February, the 42nd of Shinka Era,
 Haneda Airport)

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.020
A bomb exploded in a restroom
 in Haneda Airport,

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.260
and the area is still
 in turmoil even at night.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.260
The Metropolitan Police Department...

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.850
They found bombs on bullet trains
 and Tokyo Station too.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.980
A plan to cover every area maybe.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.150
Not again.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.440
For the moment,
 no threats have been received.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.650
The bomber's motive and objective
 remain unknown.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.580
None? There must be evidence
 from that explosion.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:30.350
Our whole team recovered
 loads of machinery.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:32.460
Machinery? Not a bomb?

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.440
No. But they were taken
 due to executive orders.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.470
Here's all the evidence
 from the explosion.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.470
A security robot blown to bits.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.600
The fourth attack on
 Yatsuka Heavy Industry people.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.020
Why the Superhuman Bureau again?

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.270
We have investigating rights
 for criminal cases, right?

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:03.150
If the explosions weren't random,

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:05.850
then departing passengers
 were targeted.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.730
There isn't anybody by that name here.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.230
That can't be.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:12.810
Someone injured in the explosion

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:16.350
wrote at the hospital he
 worked at Yatsuka's Kamata Lab.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.980
But he's been missing since.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:21.810
Wait, stop!

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:25.600
To be safe,
 we had the lab move to the country

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:27.150
Good work.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.690
Yatsuka is the key of
 Japan's heavy industries.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.850
People involved in it are attacked.
 Who is the enemy?

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.520
Rumor has it that Yatsuka develops
 robot weapons for other countries.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.100
Just research is legal.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.450
What if they completed
 a robot weapon,

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.700
and somebody is trying to
 stop them from war use.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.440
That's like a heroic superhuman.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.440
But they're doing
 serial corporate bombings.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.350
It's caused damages too.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:03.060
I'm shocked to hear it was a bomb.
 That was terrorism.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.470
So you're saying somebody
 attacked Yatsuka scientists, yes?

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:11.560
The Japanese people's
 suitcase transformed.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.600
I wish I had that camera.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:19.480
I exchanged the witness' camera
 with the latest German model.

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.600
- Hey, ghost.
 - Got it.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:24.910
And finally.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:30.870
This shadow attacked the Yatsuka
 employees headed for America.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.150
They hastily activated
 their security robot but...

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:36.380
Bang! In one hit.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.650
He's dangerous.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.850
I want to talk.
 There must be a reason.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:47.400
To protect superhumans and
 manage them. That's our job.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.310
I'm looking for
 Yatsuka attacker evidence.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.190
- No more radio fees.
 - It's hidden here...

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.400
- It's the TV era now.
 - What?

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.060
Hello, Detective Shiba.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.650
What, a detective?

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.870
I haven't done anything.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:13.040
You've got more weirdos
 since I last saw you.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.060
Fuurouta, the ghost.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:19.040
And her? A young girl
 at a place like this?

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:24.170
Why don't you join us?
 Police work must be pretty hard.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.270
Especially with the recent protests.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:29.300
I won't join
 the indecent Superhuman Bureau.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.100
He said indecent.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.400
I don't get it.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.680
I'm no rodent!

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.440
Attacks?

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:40.060
Haneda was a bombing
 by a mad bomber, no?

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.610
You used your power to make them
 say that, as usual.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:48.100
The attacker was superhuman,
 so you hide the truth.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:52.740
What if Yatsuka is evil and
 it's a heroic superhuman fighting it?

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:55.150
That's just Jiro's imagination.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.940
Or rather, his desire.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:00.600
I told you.
 Heroic superhuman don't exist.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:05.230
What exists are monsters that
 have or will cause trouble.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:07.480
We will find the attacker.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.560
I'll defeat it before that.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.640
I have that authority.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:18.140
He used to be
 a brilliant young detective.

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:21.600
But he was killed by
 an evil organization.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:24.350
Then a genius scientist, for fun,

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.150
planted his memory and personality
 into his new body.

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:29.700
He's a robot?

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.650
He wanted to continue
 being a detective,

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:36.900
as the one and only policeman
 dedicated to superhuman cases.

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:39.400
Superhuman Bureau...

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:44.270
Superhumans fulfill selfish wishes
 using illegal destructive powers.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:46.270
What justice can be in that?

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:53.350
Farewell, my dear lover.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.940
Precious memories...

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:01.020
Sorry, I thought I was alone.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.360
Not at all. I like that song too.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:09.020
I release my electric brain's heat
 by converting it to sound waves.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.600
What would she do if I said that?

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:15.690
Are you with Yatsuka Heavy Industry?
 The new factory there.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:17.100
Uh, no.

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.060
It's dangerous. Run.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.100
You...

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:30.900
What's happening to me?

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:32.600
Run, hurry!

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.650
He... He's here.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.230
You are...?

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.190
Mr. Jaguar, is it her?

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.230
You two are too soft!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.650
I'm no enemy.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.310
This girl...

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:57.580
What are you...?

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:00.400
Should I stop time?

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.830
But too many uncertainties.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.580
- They're here!
 - Get the load.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:07.350
Let go of me.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:11.190
Answer me. Did you do Haneda
 and before too?

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:12.560
I'm sorry.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.100
It's not him.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:37.810
But what has his smell...

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:39.900
I won't let it go to war.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:41.810
No!

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:44.690
Stop!

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.020
- Kikko!
 - Got it.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.400
Meteortail!

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.360
Jiro, the car. After them!

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.400
Hey.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:16.490
Are you okay?

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:18.620
He's a robot, leave him.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:22.040
He's a superhuman too.
 The Bureau will protect him.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:24.230
Hey, who are you guys?

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:25.350
Come with us.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.190
Stop it.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:28.560
I...

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:32.900
(I'm not superhuman. I'm human.)

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:39.550
I gathered and brought them to Japan.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:55.200
The only person discovered at Guam
 was him. You never existed.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:57.780
Why come home after all this time?

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:02.330
Who are you?

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.200
I'd been waiting for you.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.250
Waiting? Who are you?

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:17.090
Raito Shiba. Former First
 Investigation Division detective.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.910
Currently, a wanted criminal.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.910
(February, the 47st of Shinka Era)

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.220
(Former Japanese Army Sergeant
 returns, no record of others)

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:29.230
I saw that 8mm tape.
 I'm amazed it survived.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:34.000
It's surely the Type A made
 during the war at Ikuta Laboratory.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:35.370
Type A?

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:38.860
Of the pair of
 male and female andoroids?

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.500
Male and female?

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:44.290
Both andoroids had gone missing
 in the chaos after the war.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.620
One of them has been activated?

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:50.910
There was an airliner accident
 at Matsushiro the other day.

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.880
Maybe that's related.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:56.080
Either way,
 it's a valuable superhuman.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:58.380
We'll make sure to secure it.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.330
I'm coming in.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:17.480
I didn't put you in
 the Superhuman Bureau for this.

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:19.620
Forgive me, Father.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:24.240
Is it true that she was
 created during the war?

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.040
You were listening?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:29.370
No, you can't help but hear
 with those ears.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:30.870
Prof. Hitoyoshi.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:35.200
Rumors say you were in
 the Ikuta Laboratory during the war.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:36.750
You know well.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.510
But that lab no longer exists.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:44.370
It was rumored that Ikuta Laboratory
 made secret weapons.

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:49.020
But I just did research on
 strategic superhuman use.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:53.900
But why did they make
 boy and girl robots?

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:59.700
You can make them look like foreigners
 and teach them languages.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:02.280
Easy for
 infiltrating enemy countries.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:06.410
They made a boy and girl
 so they'd look like a couple.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:09.790
She said that she was looking for him.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.200
In other words,

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:15.370
the male andoroid she was
 separated from 20 years ago.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:18.420
Machine love.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:21.840
- Don't be so unscientific.
 - But...

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.410
They're machines.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:27.040
If she's looking for
 her male counterpart,

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.580
it's because they were
 made that way.

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:35.580
With you, the personality and thoughts
 of the original person is simulated.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:38.610
In that sense, you have a free mind.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:44.000
But Type A Mieko Kohrogi
 and Type B Kaoru Handa

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.080
are complete andoroids.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:50.410
So their thoughts and morals are just
 what researchers implanted.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:56.130
They were designed to want to
 search for each other and merge.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.250
Merge?

00:12:57.870 --> 00:12:58.950
What for?

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:03.380
Their feature was that merging
 would make them the ultimate weapon.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:07.260
I wasn't involved,
 so that's all I know.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.010
Become a weapon?

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:14.040
So they each infiltrate an enemy city
 as regular humans,

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:17.580
and become bombs only by merging.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.030
The ultimate weapon.

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:23.830
I don't get it.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:28.120
You're not completely fixed.
 Take it easy.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:30.410
You tampered with my body?

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.250
After the war,
 the Ikuta Laboratory research

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.540
became the basis of robot engineering.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.290
That technology
 was used in your body too.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.500
That's why Father could fix you.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:46.040
(Imperial Army Ikuta Laboratory)

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:47.750
Okay, cameras roll!

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:51.040
So she was born here.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:55.580
It seems the male Type B was sent
 south at the end of the war.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.790
Not being able to
 find her man from before...

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.450
She's a criminal taking it out
 on similar men.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.410
If you protect her,
 you have no justice.

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:08.950
You're destroying her
 is the only justice there is?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:15.620
Leave it to me.

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:30.390
Where are you going?
 Are you non-political?

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.860
Strange.
 I didn't think we'd meet again.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:46.360
It's not strange. You sought me out.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:51.120
I see. But it's not you
 who I'm searching for.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.700
I know.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.250
But your man is gone.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:07.500
A robot thought for itself
 and rebelled against its maker.

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.870
That's what I'd imagined.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.580
Like a ninja running away for justice.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:13.910
A ninja?

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:16.430
But not Miss Mieko, right?

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:18.910
She's just searching for a loved one.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:20.250
It's not love.

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.810
They were designed to seek each other.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.040
But...

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:28.410
Humans are like that too.
 They're designed to love someone.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.320
That's why they love.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:31.870
Am I wrong?

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.330
I think that's justice.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:37.700
Shiba says that destroying her
 is justice.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.920
Is there that many different kinds
 of justice?

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:46.700
That's not true.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:49.620
I'm just searching
 for that one person.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.500
But strange things
 always get in my way.

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:56.220
That's only because
 you're designed like that.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:59.080
A fake love given to you.

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:03.230
That's why you're drawn to Yatsuka's
 robots with the same technology.

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:06.290
But, I'm drawn to you too...

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:09.290
Mieko!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:17.780
I stopped time.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.250
For a radius of 100 meters.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.330
I can only stop it for
 virtually 30 seconds.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:24.790
You know what to do.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:27.660
I'm going.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:35.550
Raise your head, Equus!

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:51.910
Mr. Jaguar!

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:55.410
- Did anybody notice it?
 - Are you okay, Mr. Jaguar?

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:00.910
What's going on?

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.410
Sorry. I followed Detective Shiba.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.750
I knew you'd come to him.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:07.950
Me?

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:13.290
It seems I have the same
 basic design as your male Type B.

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.830
That's why I reacted so much to you.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:17.370
You too.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:19.660
You're just designed the same way?

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:22.700
That's enough.
 I'm using the halting device.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:24.600
Let's talk somewhere safe...

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:29.560
There's no need.
 I'll destroy her here.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.830
- Detective Shiba.
 - No one will take her.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.040
Tell me!

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:55.330
I still want to see him. Why?

00:17:56.450 --> 00:18:01.260
You're implanted with
 a desire to merge with Type B.

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:04.160
Probably to become a powerful bomb.

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:06.620
A bomb?

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:17.950
With me, you won't become a bomb.

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.200
So this is where the water plant was.

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:44.640
Yes, construction was behind schedule
 so there was still water here.

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:47.540
Soon, tons of those
 will be built here.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.160
Can you believe it?

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:54.750
5 years ago, I thought Miss Mieko
 had self-destructed.

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:59.280
But she had dived to
 the bottom reservoir layer.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.410
And she slept there.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:07.370
An acquaintance worked here,
 and contacted me right away.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:11.290
It must've been destiny for you
 to come home then.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:15.050
I knew nothing.

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:19.870
I just followed the given orders, and hid in the south.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:22.680
This country rotted away during that.

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:27.370
The justice I believed in was lost,
 and many youth died.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:30.940
So merge with Miss Mieko.

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:35.820
You two were given fake love
 and a fake sense of justice.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:39.370
I can teach you
 what real justice is now.

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:42.200
To awaken Japan right now.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.160
Why are you here?

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:53.910
Stop!

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:58.880
What are you doing? Not yet.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:01.250
What good is it to explode it here?

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:03.450
The Winter Sports Grand-Prix is it.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:06.950
In front of the world,
 the current government...

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.190
Cross-Megassing.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.520
Stop!

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.950
What's going on?

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:39.420
My father said if they merge,
 they'd be the ultimate weapon.

00:20:39.910 --> 00:20:43.500
It's not a bomb.
 It's Andoroid Megasshin.

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:47.160
Nobody knows about this superhuman.

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:51.700
If they infiltrate the venue,
 they can cause enough damage.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.330
Detective Shiba.

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:56.870
I cannot obey you.

00:20:57.660 --> 00:20:58.610
Why?

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:02.580
Mieko, I'm the one that
 brought you two together.

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:04.330
I thank you for that.

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:07.080
But what you're trying to do is evil.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.660
You're just a machine!

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:12.200
They're no machine. They're justice.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.120
They understand justice?

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.330
The scientists taught them justice.

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:20.250
To protect the country.
 To save the people.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:22.750
What righteousness is.

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:27.260
Humans interpret that on their own
 and at times make mistakes.

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:29.660
But machines obey accurately.

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:32.250
You say they're justice and I'm evil?

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:33.390
It's not me.

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:35.700
That's how they judged it.

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:58.250
Detective Shiba.

00:22:02.120 --> 00:22:05.540
I'm Raito now.
 Iron-Detective Raito!

00:22:06.370 --> 00:22:09.080
No matter who wins,
 we're no longer justice.

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:12.510
But it still has to be fought out.

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:00.910
An unexplored underground world.
 A southern island not on maps.

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:03.460
A mystical world
 ruled by those not human.

00:24:03.460 --> 00:24:07.410
Look, an explorer of uninhabited areas
 and Japan's proud intelligence.

00:24:07.420 --> 00:24:10.330
His name is Magotake.
 Magotake Hitoyoshi.
